# Hibernate Core Dependency
Step 2: Add Hibernate Dependencies in pom.xml
- Now that your Maven project is set up, let's add some dependencies. Dependencies are like ingredients for a recipe- without them, your Java app won't work.
. Open pom.xml: In your project folder, find and open the pom.xml file. This file keeps track of what your project needs.
. Add Hibernate Core and MySQL Connector: Add the following inside the <dependencies> section:

<dependencies>
<!-- Hibernate Core Dependency -- >
<dependency>
<groupld>org.hibernate</groupld>
<artifactld>hibernate-core</artifactld>
<version>5.6.9.Final</version>
</dependency>

<!-- MySQL Connector Dependency -- >
<dependency>
<groupld>mysql</groupld>
<artifactld>mysql-connector-java</artifactld>
<version>8.0.28</version>
</dependency>
</dependencies>
